   The recount applies each state's on/off rules to the PS-IDLE-SPEC rows with each row's own conversion factor
   (battery W over load W in PS-IDLE-SPEC) and does not re-solve the distribution I2R at the lower current, which
   is why it reads a few tenths of a watt above the model in the reduced states (the model's I2R at 31 W is
   about 0.1 W, at 43 W about 0.2 W). The 'D rows at makers' figures' column replaces the five declared rows
   (panel board C, other +3V3_DEV logic, board E controller, board A logic, four CP2102N bridges) by the sum of
   the makers' typical supply currents d4energy read for the same parts, and the board D row by the maker's
   figure where it is HIGHER than the declaration: the declarations are copper-sizing allocations, and the
   difference (about 3 W) is what the bench must settle; the balance below runs at the model's PLAN figures and
   never at the lower ones (nothing is lowered to obtain a result).

2. USABLE BATTERY ENERGY of the ruled 4S3P block (12 x Samsung INR18650-35E)

   E = 12 cells x C_min x f_rate(I) x f_T x V_mean(I) x f_dod x f_age, at the state's constant power:
   C_min 3.35 Ah (spec 3.1, 0.2C to 2.65 V at 23 C); f_rate spec 7.8 (100 percent at 0.68 A, 97 at 3.4 A, linear);
   f_T spec 7.5 (40 / 97 at -10 C at 3.4 A, 1.00 at 20 to 40 C; between -10 and 20 C linear, INFERRED, a lower
   bound at the kit's currents); V_mean the typical cell's Wh / Ah of the Technical Report (3.624 V at 0.2C, 3.443 V
   at 3.5 A, linear); f_dod the share of the trace delivered when the cell reaches the graceful line of 3.00 V
   under load (0.937 at 0.7 A, 0.905 at 3.5 A, an AI reading of the maker's traces) or the 5 percent RSOC
   reserve, whichever comes first (the voltage line does, at every current here); f_age 0.80 (REQ-014, SC-23) or
   0.60 (spec 7.9, the lower bracket). Nominal: 12 x 3.35 x 3.60 = 144.7 Wh.

