   Reading the table: a 100 Wp panel never reaches the window (its peak is under 100 W) and gives 320 Wh a day at the
   node in September and 90 in December (the low brackets 251 and 70). A larger panel is clipped at 100 W into
   the stage for the hours shown, and the most the window can pass in a day is 85 W x the lit hours: 1102 Wh in
   September and 678 Wh in December with a panel large enough to hold the clip all day. That is the ceiling a
   re-rated input path (S-53) would lift; the fuse F2 and J_SOLAR at 10 A carry two paralleled 100 Wp panels'
   short-circuit current (about 12.5 A) NOT, so more than about 150 Wp of 12 V class panel also re-rates the entry.

