    OFF: slots 1 and 2 with their fans, PCIe switches and drives; both WiFi link cards; the 5G module (no host on
    slot 3); the monitor and HDMI 5 V; the SDR, the camera, the QMX, the Geiger (deferred by D-01); the E72 pair;
    the mixer fans (a shaded, cool night; on in the heat). Battery-side 15.7 W PLAN (13.1 W with the D rows at
    the makers' figures); the aged pack carries it 7.0 h at +20 C (8.4 h at the sourced figure), against
    September's 11.3 h of sun-down and 16 h of sun below the load (100 Wp). It does not carry a September night alone.
    What it changes: firmware and operator settings only (the KSZ energy-detect mode and the supervisors' 200 MHz
    clock are firmware items to confirm on the generated boards); it is the heat stage after BANK-R1 with six
    loads off or lowered, so it needs BANK-R1 in board B's generator (CONOPS 4c). Cost: none in parts. Mission:
    the monitor, the WiFi link, 5G and Zigbee are dark at night; the e-paper and the panel lamps carry the status.

6b. The usable depth of discharge: the graceful line 3.00 V to 2.80 V under load gains 1.9 Wh aged (108 to 110 Wh);
    the 5 percent RSOC reserve then ends the run first at low currents (f_dod capped at 0.95). Cost: none; a
    gauge image and bridge setting (CONOPS 4c's PROVISIONAL threshold). Mission: about 3 minutes more at
    PS-IDLE-SPEC, 7 at the night state; cycle life is the maker's question (the cycle test discharges to 2.65 V).

6c. Cells in the east pocket (58 x 240 x 47.9 mm; A06's fit study on the committed board B underside):
  configuration         nominal Wh  east pocket                                                                                                          west pocket                                      
  --------------------  ----------  -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------  -------------------------------------------------
  4S3P 18650, 12 cells  144.7       FITS as a shrink-wrapped block with board P at its end (X spare 1.35, Z clear 4.53 nominal, 3.32 at the worst base)  NO (X spare -17.42 with board P beside the cells)
  4S4P 18650, 16 cells  193.0       NO (X spare -17.42 in the nearest arrangement)                                                                       NO                                               
