  1. night state (a) + 2.80 V line (b) + second 4S3P pack (d), 100 Wp, 100 W window  NOT MET: night asks 251 Wh (15.7 W x 16 h), two packs hold 221  MET: night asks 220 Wh (15.7 W x 14 h), two packs hold 221      NOT MET: night asks 345 Wh (15.7 W x 22 h), two packs hold 156
  2. as 1 with a 200 Wp panel in the 100 W window                                    MET: night asks 220 Wh (15.7 W x 14 h), two packs hold 221      MET: night asks 188 Wh (15.7 W x 12 h), two packs hold 221      NOT MET: night asks 283 Wh (15.7 W x 18 h), two packs hold 156
  3. as 1 with the path re-rated to 300 W and a 330 Wp panel (e)                     MET: night asks 220 Wh (15.7 W x 14 h), two packs hold 221      MET: night asks 173 Wh (15.7 W x 11 h), two packs hold 221      NOT MET: night asks 283 Wh (15.7 W x 18 h), two packs hold 156
  4. heat stage PS-SURV-R at night + (b) + second pack + re-rated path and 330 Wp    NOT MET: night asks 326 Wh (23.3 W x 14 h), two packs hold 221  NOT MET: night asks 279 Wh (23.3 W x 12 h), two packs hold 221  NOT MET: night asks 419 Wh (23.3 W x 18 h), two packs hold 156
  5. reduced mode PS-RED2 at night + (b) + second pack + re-rated path and 330 Wp    NOT MET: night asks 439 Wh (31.4 W x 14 h), two packs hold 221  NOT MET: night asks 377 Wh (31.4 W x 12 h), two packs hold 221  NOT MET: night asks 565 Wh (31.4 W x 18 h), two packs hold 156
  6. PS-IDLE-SPEC as written + (b) + second pack + re-rated path and 330 Wp          NOT MET: night asks 599 Wh (42.8 W x 14 h), two packs hold 219  NOT MET: night asks 556 Wh (42.8 W x 13 h), two packs hold 219  NOT MET: night asks 856 Wh (42.8 W x 20 h), two packs hold 155

   'MET' is the hour-by-hour run ending above the graceful threshold with no stop; the ask and the hold beside
   it are the one-night arithmetic that explains it (a run can pass with the ask slightly above the hold when
   the sun charges the packs part way through the deficit hours, and fail the other way when December's
   cold cells hold less).
END. REQ-072's verdict on these figures: FAIL (unchanged); see ENERGY-RECONCILIATION.md sections 5 and 7.
